## Block scoping

```js
function example() {
  var x = 'function scoped';
  let y = 'block scoped';

  if (true) {
    var x = 'still same x'; // overwrites outer x!
    let y = 'different y';  // new binding, only in this block
    console.log(y); // 'different y'
  }

  console.log(x); // 'still same x' — var leaked out
  console.log(y); // 'block scoped'  — let did not
}
```

## Temporal Dead Zone

```js
console.log(a); // undefined — var is hoisted and initialised
console.log(b); // ReferenceError — let is in TDZ
var a = 1;
let b = 2;
```

## No re-declaration

```js
var v = 1;
var v = 2; // fine with var

let l = 1;
let l = 2; // SyntaxError: Identifier 'l' has already been declared
```

## let vs const

```js
let count = 0;
count++;          // ✅ let can be reassigned

const MAX = 100;
MAX = 200;        // ❌ TypeError: Assignment to constant variable

const obj = {};
obj.x = 1;        // ✅ const prevents rebinding, not mutation
```

